Only dig out paths on the no-teleport levels.

Make sure you have teleport control and teleportitis.  Save most of
those ?teleportation you find in huge quantities for the trek back up.
You'll normally have several spare /digging (on top of saving 5
(plenty) for Earth).

If you're a spellcaster, you might want to save some PW for combat.
Save !gain energy and write up some b?charging.  On the hike up, use ^T
to teleport until you're out of PW (non-caster) or maybe halfway down
(caster who's saving some for combat).  Use scrolls after that, you'll
be recharging PW while using scrolls to climb.  If it's just a short
trek to the stairs, walk it.  If you're out of PW and scrolls, either
dig (if a couple zaps will get you an easy path) or just walk it while
waiting for teleportitis to kick in.

Save and curse all the !gain level you find (I'll sometimes use some to
reach XL14 if I'm unlucky w/ wraiths and such).  Use one out of the
sanctum (which hopefully you levelported into in the first place to
avoid slogging through the graveyard and other beasts).  Use the others
for the no-teleport levels with nasty hikes (asmodeus, baalzebub, etc).
 You can dig through the wall next to the stairs in Orcus Town, so that
shortens things a bit.



